\lispPackageChapter{livermore/csv}

The \texttt{livermore/csv} package reads comma-separated files into lists of
lists.  Numbers are parsed with \texttt{read-from-string}; everything else
is left as a string.  The first row is not treated as a header.

\section{Parameters}

\lispParameterSubsection{*separator*}

The column separator.  Default comma.

\lispParameterSubsection{*quote*}

The string delimiter.  Default the double-quote character.  A quote is
closed by a second quote; escaped quotes inside a field are not supported.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{character-list-from-stream}

Reads every character from \lispVar{stream} until the stream ends.

\lispFunctionSubsection{parse-character-list}

The parser.  Returns a list of rows, each a list of fields.

\lispFunctionSubsection{parse-stream}

Reads a stream and parses it.

\lispFunctionSubsection{parse-file}

Opens \lispVar{pathname} and parses it.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(parse-file \lispVar{pathname})}
